Here's how you use axios with React:

1. Install axios:

```
npm install axios
```

2. Import axios in your React component:

```jsx
import axios from 'axios';
```

3. Make API calls in your component's methods:

```jsx
getUsers = () => {
  axios.get('https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users')
    .then(res => {
      const users = res.data;
      // Update state with users data
      this.setState({ users });
    })
}
```

4. Call the method on component mount:

```jsx
componentDidMount() {
  this.getUsers();
}
```

5. Render the data:

```jsx
render() {
  return (
    {this.state.users.map(user => {
      return (
        <div key={user.id}>
          {user.name} 
        </div>
      );
    })}
  );   
}
```

This will make an API call on component mount, fetch the list of users, and render each user's name in a div.

You can make GET, POST, PUT, DELETE requests using `axios.get()`, `axios.post()`, `axios.put()` and `axios.delete()` respectively.

